  "comment": "The time left to a job's next run, as the Board shows it (docs/project-board-tui-plan.md, cron). `now` is local wall-clock time with seconds and `next` a local minute (a `next_run`), both without a zone. The difference is rounded UP to whole minutes, then the largest unit that fits is kept and rounded down: 1440 minutes or more is Nd, 60 minutes or more is Nh, otherwise Nm. A difference of zero or less is 0m. Written by hand; the Python window (project_board.model.remaining_text) and the Rust sidebar both read this file.",
